   "rawText": "Additional Courses: Require a grade of C or better\nSelect 3 credits from the following:3\nBIOL 141Introduction to Human Physiology\nBIOL 161Human Anatomy and Physiology I - Lecture\nBISC 4Human Body: Form and Function\nAt least 15 credits of the following courses must be at the 400 level:\nSelect 4 credits from the following:4\nCategory 1 (Statistics)\nPSYCH 200Elementary Statistics in Psychology\nor STAT 200 Elementary Statistics\nSelect 6 credits from two different developmental categories (3 credits each category):6\nCategory 2a (Lifespan)\nPSYCH 212Introduction to Developmental Psychology\nCategory 2b (Adult)\nPSYCH 416/HDFS 445Development Throughout Adulthood\nCategory 2c (Child)\nPSYCH 410Child Development\nCategory 2d (Adolescence)\nPSYCH 412Adolescence\nSelect 6 credits from two different individual difference categories (3 credits each category):6\nCategory 3a (Social Psychology)\nPSYCH 221Introduction to Social Psychology\nor PSYCH 420 Advanced Social Psychology\nCategory 3b (Personality Psychology)\nPSYCH 238Introduction to Personality Psychology\nor PSYCH 438 Personality Theory\nCategory 3c (Personal Adjustment)\nPSYCH 243Introduction to Well-being and Positive Psychology\nor PSYCH 471 Psychology of Adjustment and Social Relationships\nCategory 3d (Health Psychology)\nPSYCH 441Health Psychology\nSelect 6 credits from two different clinical categories (3 credits each category):6\nCategory 4a (Physical Disabilities)\nPSYCH 370Psychology of the Differently-Abled\nCategory 4b (Childhood Disorders)\nPSYCH 476Child Psychopathology\nCategory 4c (Abnormal Psychology)\nPSYCH 270Introduction to Abnormal Psychology\nor PSYCH 470 Abnormal Psychology\nCategory 4d (Behavior Modification)\nPSYCH 473Behavior Modification\nCategory 4e (Developmental Disabilities)\nPSYCH 443Treatment and Education in Developmental Disabilities\nSelect 6 credits from two different experimental categories (3 credits in each category):6\nCategory 5a (Physiological Psychology)\nPSYCH 260/BBH 203Neurological Bases of Human Behavior\nor PSYCH 462 Physiological Psychology\nCategory 5b (Cognitive Psychology)\nPSYCH 256Introduction to Cognitive Psychology\nor PSYCH 452 Learning and Memory\nor PSYCH 456 Advanced Cognitive Psychology\nCategory 5c (Learning Theory)\nPSYCH 261Introduction to Psychology of Learning\nor PSYCH 461 Advanced Conditioning and Learning\nSelect 3 credits from applications in psychology:3\nCategory 6 (Applied Experience)\nPSYCH 395Internship\nor PSYCH 494 Research Projects\nor PSYCH 495 Internship\nSelect 12 credits of any PSYCH courses not used above, with the exception that only one course selected from any Category 1 through 5 will count for the major12\n"
